Count the contexts alive in ANGLEMetalMemoryLine (Minato, patch 0031).

Why: an app that loses its GL context's thread at a return can make a new context and never destroy the old one (SDL
2 on Android, when the app resets its display before SDL restores the context it backed up). Each such context keeps
its GL objects, so the memory grows by a context's textures per return, and no line said why. Now ContextMtl counts
itself from its construction until ANGLE destroys it (eglDestroyContext, once no thread has it current), and the
memory line appends " ctx=<n>" after mtl=.
Test: graphics/tests/angle_memory_counters.mm (ctx=1 with the test's context, 2 with one more made and never current,
1 again once that one is destroyed, 0 once the test's own is released and destroyed).
Upstream: not planned (an embedder's diagnostic).
diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/metal/ContextMtl.mm
@@ -200,9 +200,15 @@
       mDriverUniforms{},
       mProvokingVertexHelper(this),
       mContextDevice(GetOwnershipIdentity(attribs))
-{}
+{
+    // Minato (patch 0031): counted until ANGLE destroys it (eglDestroyContext, once no thread has it current).
+    mtl::NoteContextsAlive(1);
+}
 
-ContextMtl::~ContextMtl() {}
+ContextMtl::~ContextMtl()
+{
+    mtl::NoteContextsAlive(-1);
+}
 
 angle::Result ContextMtl::initialize(const angle::ImageLoadContext &imageLoadContext)
 {
